				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1741,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Standardize event naming and implement blocking notification logic\n\nCorrect the Tauri event suffix for webview messages across `GenericNotification` handlers, changing \"post-message\" to \"postMessage\" to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention. Update the fallback notification router in `MountainVinegRPCService` to sanitize event names by replacing dots with slashes, ensuring compatibility with Tauri's strict character set requirements for event identifiers.\n\nRefactor the `Window.ShowMessage` effect in `WindowUI` to support blocking behavior. Replace the fire-and-forget timestamp-based ID generation with a thread-safe atomic sequence counter for request identification. When action items are present, the handler now emits a `show-message-request` event to the `INotificationService`, registers a pending request in the application state, and awaits a one-shot channel response. This enables the UI to render action buttons and return the user's selection to the extension host, replacing the previous non-interactive implementation.\n\nThese changes ensure consistent event naming, prevent illegal event name crashes, and restore full interactivity for notification actions in the extension host IPC layer.",
			"SHA": "cb905d7a9fcd21ff5161c4316b9757f4e2adeaa2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:39:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1741,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement unregisterExternalUriOpener and unregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver notifications\n\nRegister two new gRPC notification handlers in `MountainVinegRPCService` to support the disposal of external URI opener and remote authority resolver handles defined in the Vine protocol.\n\nCreate dedicated notification modules `UnregisterExternalUriOpener` and `UnregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver` within `Source/Vine/Server/Notification/`. Both modules leverage the existing `UnregisterByHandle` helper to perform the cleanup logic, ensuring consistent registration state management across the extension host IPC layer.\n\nThese changes extend the Mountain backend to fully support the lifecycle management of remote authority and URI opener extensions via the gRPC interface.",
			"SHA": "9c72840ca6348b0f64076aa13e4b742ec13dcbd5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:35:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add webview.setOptions support and align postMessage event naming\n\nRegister the new `webview.setOptions` handler within the `MountainVinegRPCService` routing logic to enable configuration updates for Tauri webviews. This expands the IPC surface to match the updated Vine protocol requirements.\n\nIn the `CreateEffectForRequest` tracker, correct the event suffix mapping for the `postMessage` command. Restore the PascalCase naming convention by changing the target event string from \"post-message\" to \"postMessage\". This ensures consistency with the project-wide PascalCase naming standard for all UI-to-Rust event identifiers.\n\nThese changes complete the `setOptions` integration and resolve an event naming inconsistency in the webview effect registry.",
			"SHA": "948a6514d4e201dc15936998f5375a0064360d9b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:19:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Restore ShowMessageBox text composition and multi-select return\n\nThe `ShowMessageBox` handler incorrectly relied on a non-existent `.body()` method, causing the detail text to overwrite the dialog title entirely. Update the implementation to concatenate the message and detail text with a newline separator before passing to the native dialog constructor, preserving the original title.\n\nIn `QuickInputShowQuickPick`, refactor the multi-select logic to extract the `CanPickMany` flag prior to consuming the options struct. This ensures the return value correctly returns the full array of selected labels for multi-select operations instead of silently discarding all but the first selection.\n\nAdditionally, remove the `showTextDocument` effect from `Workspace` IPC routing. This handler is obsolete as the functionality is now covered by the dedicated Sky UI service implementation, preventing redundant or conflicting event dispatching from the extension host.\n\nThese changes restore native dialog usability, fix multi-selection in quick pick inputs, and streamline the IPC effect registry.",
			"SHA": "a499709153a4b0c357a78ab80630f38989bea10e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:01:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Correct output channel payload structure for Sky integration\n\nThe `CreateOutputChannel` gRPC handler previously emitted an IPC event with a single `{ \"channel\": name }` property. Sky's `InstallEditorAndOutput.ts` component expects the payload to destructure `{ id, name }`. The mismatch caused both fields to resolve as undefined in the frontend map, keyed incorrectly by the string \"undefined\".\n\nUpdate the Tauri event emission to include both `id` and `name` fields set to `Request.name`. This aligns the Mountain backend output with the Sky component's destructuring logic, ensuring new output channels are correctly registered and displayed in the editor UI.",
			"SHA": "930ce3222f11418b22c721b91133d0b33e55474a"
		}
	],
